cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this project, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Evaluating Typo-Robust Product Retrieval for Hinglish E-Commerce Queries: A Comparative Synthetic Pilot Study"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Harkirat
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-25
repository-code: "https://github.com/harkirat871/hinglish-product-retrieval-study"
abstract: >-
  A reproducible synthetic pilot study comparing BM25, character n-gram TF-IDF,
  and hybrid Reciprocal Rank Fusion on Roman-script Hinglish-style automotive
  product queries with controlled spelling variation. The catalog and queries
  are synthetic; the study does not use real customer messages or verified
  product-compatibility records.
keywords:
  - Hinglish
  - code-mixing
  - information retrieval
  - e-commerce search
  - spelling variation
  - synthetic dataset
